@node Requirements " System-requirements of Task-NewScan"
                               
                           What do you need is:

                              an Amiga Model 
       [ 500 600 1000 1200 2000 2500 3000 4030 4040 5000 CDTV CD³² ]
               Kickstart 2.xx / 3.xx   Workbench 2.xx / 3.xx
                        AmiExpress V3.xx / V4.xx
                             User and uploads

                            @{" Go back to main " Link MAIN}

@endnode                                                                                 
@node Installation " Installation of Task-NewScan"

Extract the archive [TK-NS001.LHA] and copy them to the right places...

The Arcive include:  BBS:DOORS/Task-NewScan/Task-NewScan
                     BBS:COMMANDS/BBSCMD/N.INFO
                     BBS:COMMANDS/BBSCMD/F.INFO
                     BBS:COMMANDS/SYSCMD/N.INFO


                     @{" Go on to the tooltypes " Link tooltypes}
@endnode
@node Tooltypes " Tooltypes of the Task-NewScan"

             Only the N.INFO and the F.INFO needs TOOLTYPES...
                       Both icons need the same ....

                 LOCATION=Doors:Task-NewScan/Task-NewScan
                 MULTINODE=YES                           
                 ACCESS=1                             
                 TYPE=XIM
                 NAME=Task-NewScan

               - Be sure, that your DOOR-DIR is assigned ! -


                    @{" How to make this door resident ?? " Link resident}
                            @{" Go back to main " Link MAIN}
@endnode
@node resident " How to make task-NewScan RESIDENT ?? "

               You can also make this Task-Scan resident...
          If you want to make this door resident, then insert the
              following tooltypes in all icons of this scan:
   [ BBS:COMMANDS/BBSCMD/N.INFO ,  F.INFO ; BBS:COMMANDS/SYSCMD/N.INFO ]

                 LOCATION=Task-NewScan
                 RESIDENT
                 MULTINODE=YES
                 ACCESS=1
                 TYPE=XIM
                 NAME=Task-NewScan

  Protect the TASK-NEWSCAN in our doors with --P-RWED to make it residentable
         Then go to our user-startup and add the following string:

                 Resident Doors:TASK-NEWSCAN/TASK-NEWSCAN

   Reboot your mashine or just enter the shell and just type in the same
                          to make it resident !!

                            @{" Go back to main " Link MAIN}
@endnode
@node WhatisT-NS " What Is Task-NewScan ??? "

                      Task-NewScan is a product from 
                         @{" SvEN tHE CREAToR " Link ich}
   it`s a replacement for any NEWFILES...it`s not only a replacement...
                         this is a NEWFILES...hehe

                  @{" What can I and the users do ??? " Link Usercando}
@endnode
@node Usercando " What can the sysop and the users do ??? "

  The extraordinary of this tool is the BACKSCROLLING of the FILELIST...
  ALL newfiles are able to scroll from the begining to the end...but the 
    Task-NewScan is able to scroll up and down...to jump up and down...

                       @{" How can i test it ??? " Link Howcanitestit}
@endnode
@node Howcanitestit " How can i test Task-NewScan ??? "

                           How can i test it ???

hehehe...sipmly question...heavy answer....first...be sure , that you have
   the right lines of your screen...if you are not sure...check them...
( Press `W` and then the `5`...and just type the Number , you see at the top)

Now you must log in into our BBS...and start the Task-NewScan ( Start it with
 `N`...if you DON`T KNOW IT )...you see...it`s working..now Task-NewScan 
 (I`ll will short it with T-NS) ask for the date...now you can type in the
                        date for begin scanning....

Ex.:                    08-07-94 [ MONTH-DAY-YEAR ]

  OR..you can type in the day to scan back...like -2 for two days back !

  Now T-NS asks for the dir....type in one of our dir...or simply `U` for
   Upload-Dir....User with a security-Level higher than 200 are allowed
                     to scan the Hold-Dir with `H` !!

For the expert User, you can start the T-NS with N -2 or how do you like...
      You can write the options of the T-NS WITHOUT any direction...
                  Do you understand ??? No ???? Look....
______________________________________________________________________________
fACElESS wORLD #1 [5:/X-tOOLS] Menu (14367 mins. left): N  A   NS      -2
¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯
     You see...T-NS isn`t specified of the order of the options....you
       can also put SPACES between the options...the T-NS will scan
      the uploads to days back in all dirs with nonstop....try it...

Now T-NS starts Scanning...and HOW FAST..gelle ?? now...the first Files will
     be displayed...now..look at the end of this screen..you see this:

Enter command: C,F,N,S,Q,UP,DN,LF,RG,BS,1-3,7-9,?,CR :      [000%] Flags: None

                     This are the commands of the T-NS

                    @{" T-NS - COMMANDS WHILE FILESCANNING " Link Command-?}
                    @{" T-NS - OPTIONS WITH THE COMMAND N  " Link Command-N}
                    @{" T-NS - OPTIONS WITH THE COMMAND F  " Link Command-F}

